# Monomorphic recursion: an unannotated recursive function where all return
# paths produce a consistent type. The type checker must allow this without
# requiring an explicit `fn@ReturnType` annotation.
# All code paths return Int: base case is IntLiteral(1), recursive path is
# Int because [if [= n 0] 1 [factorial [- n 1]]] returns Int in both branches
# once the recursion bottoms out.
[
  factorial: [fn [n@Int]
    [if [= n 0]
      1
      [factorial [- n 1]]
    ]
  ]
  result: [factorial 5]
]
=== out
Dict({"factorial": Function(), "result": Int(120)})
